findings.body:
The listener now only runs when V1 `ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ` is enabled. Under V2 nothing cleans up when a client is deleted:
- the per-client resource (named after the client id) stays in the admin-permissions client;
- scope permissions referencing that resource stay as well;
- those permissions keep pointing at a non-existent client.

If V1 and V2 are both enabled, `management()` returns `MgmtPermissionsV2`. Its `clients().setPermissionsEnabled` throws `UnsupportedOperationException`, so deleting a client would fail.
